# Misc
# `scripts/` stays out of the image EXCEPT `scripts/admin/`, which the
# builder stage bundles with esbuild (see Dockerfile). That directory holds
# the invite / break-glass account CLI: self-service registration is
# retired, so if Authentik OIDC is misconfigured this is the ONLY way to
# create an account — it has to be reachable from the deployed image.
#
# `scripts/importer/` deliberately stays excluded. Its modules import
# `@prisma/v1-client`, a SECOND Prisma client generated on demand from
# `prisma/v1/schema.v1.prisma` (`npm run db:generate:v1`) and absent from
# the image build — and because `next build` type-checks everything in the
# tsconfig include set, re-including it fails the build outright with
# "Cannot find module '@prisma/v1-client'". It also could not run in-cluster
# without a v1 dump to read. Generating the v1 client in the builder stage
# is the only way to ship it, and there is currently nothing for it to
# import.
#
# The `**` form matters: Docker applies every pattern and takes the last
# match, so the negation has to be able to match the nested paths.
scripts/**
!scripts/admin/**
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
